+
+## 1. Headline
+
+The P0-critical label is a mis-calibration for this row: **the core test suite is green and has never run in the failing job**. Core's `ci.yml` splits into two mutually exclusive jobs — `test` ("🧪 Core Pytest & Lint") is gated `if: github.event_name == 'push' || 'pull_request' || (dispatch && inputs.run_autofix != true)`, while `autofix` ("🔧 PyErrorFix Engine") is gated `if: github.event_name == 'schedule' || (dispatch && inputs.run_autofix == true)`. Every nightly **schedule** run executes ONLY the autofix job; every **push** run executes ONLY the test job. Four consecutive nightly runs (10-27 → 10-30) failed while same-day push runs passed — including a **clean differential pair on the identical commit `419a838`**: push (10-26T20:33Z) = success, schedule (10-27T07:23Z) = failure. The failing sidecar is structurally guaranteed to fail nightly regardless of code content.
+
